<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="06">
<name>Brake</name>
<section id="1002J_S000U" variety="S000U">
<name>Brake Control</name>
<ttl id="1002J_S000U_744TG_T0089" variety="T0089">
<name>ABS with EBD &amp; TRC &amp; VSC &amp; BA System</name>
<para id="RM00000060F00PX" category="C" type-id="300F4" name-id="442OK-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>C1231/31</dtccode>
<dtcname>Steering Angle Sensor System Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000060F00PX_05" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NU00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The skid control computer (built into the actuator) receives the steering sensor signal via CAN communication.</ptxt>
<ptxt>If there is a malfunction in the communication line to the steering sensor, DTC "U0126/63 (Steering Angle Sensor Communication Malfunction)" is output.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.53in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.86in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.69in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Output Related Items</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1231/31</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>When an abnormal signal from the steering sensor is received with IG1 terminal voltage at 9.5to17.4V</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Open or short in steering sensor power source circuit</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Steering Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Actuator assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060F00PX_06" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NV00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C129614J06" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060F00PX_07" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000060F00PX_08" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM00000060F00PX_08_0011" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NW00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Check DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000060000PX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG OFF.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON again and check that no CAN communication malfunction DTC is output. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000060000PX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Drive at 35km/h or more and turn the steering wheel, and check that no speed sensor malfunction or yaw rate sensor malfunction DTC is output. (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM00000060000PX"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title/>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.28in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.85in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>No CAN communication malfunction, speed sensor malfunction or yaw rate sensor malfunction code is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>CAN communication malfunction code is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<ptxt>Speed sensor or yaw rate sensor malfunction code is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If there is a malfunction in the speed sensor or yaw rate sensor, an abnormal value may be output even if the steering sensor is normal.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If speed sensor or yaw rate sensor malfunction codes are output at the same time, repair them and then inspect the steering sensor.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060F00PX_08_0012" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM00000060F00PX_08_0014" fin="true">B</right>
<right ref="RM00000060F00PX_08_0015" fin="true">C</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060F00PX_08_0012" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NX00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Steering Sensor Power Source System)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the steering sensor connector is free of malfunctions such as loose engagement or disconnection.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the steering sensor connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the connector case and terminals are free of deformation and corrosion.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>No deformation or corrosion</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If there is a malfunction in the steering sensor connector, replace the sensor.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage and resistance between the wire harness side connector of the steering sensor and body ground.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146385J07" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.90in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.14in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4 (IG) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>5 (BAT) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.89in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.16in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 (ESS) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000060F00PX_08_0013" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000060F00PX_08_0016" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060F00PX_08_0013">
<testtitle>Replace Steering Sensor<xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000305A000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060F00PX_08_0014">
<testtitle>Go to CAN communication system troubleshooting</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060F00PX_08_0015">
<testtitle>Go to Relevant DTC</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000060F00PX_08_0016">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>